Last spring my sister and I took the night train from Vienna to Venice.
Dr. Rossi, an old friend of the family, met us at the station with a paper map and a flask of tea.
We didn't sleep much, because the carriage rattled and the window wouldn’t close all the way.
In the morning a girl in the next seat practised her Mandarin and kept saying 你好 and 谢谢 to everyone who smiled at her.
The hotel was small,quiet and painted a pale shade of green.
Cat lovers would like it there, because a cat sleeps on the front step all day.
Our room was 4B on the third floor, so we carried the bags up 52 stairs.
Is there a better breakfast than warm bread, figs and strong coffee?
On the second day we walked 2.5 kilometres along the canals and got lost twice!
Before we left, Mr. Bianchi from the front desk wrote 再见 on a postcard and gave it to us.
